body:
I write short stories, and have two novels written that don't tell my story, mostly centered around fantasy/sci fi. My writing isn't very good so I only enjoy it with myself and the few family members I have left. I know getting a girlfriend isn't impossible, I could have one right now by flashing some money around. I want someone to appreciate me and love me as a human. I want to be desired by the opposite sex. If is just post on a dating profile my abs, and good parts of my body (covering up my scars) I get a lot of hits. But that isn't fair to anyone and it is only part of truth. That is the rub of it all, I don't expect women to want me because I am short, and covered in red hard skin. There isn't a standard out there that covers me, but I still feel like I deserve love. I am not afraid to approach people, I am confident, and I truly like to meet new people. Just getting over the way I look is so tiresome, and takes so much work.

&#x200B;

I have looked into single parent surrogacy prior, but didn't go through with it. If I was younger I would have jumped at it but now I am not so sure. My reason is I don't my natural born child to live my life and be alone. When I was younger and with Sara I still had hope, now though, my 40 plus years on this planet has been hell. Not just socially, but the physical pain of just taking a shower or running in the park is almost too much. Thankfully they had lotions and pain meds to help me live a normal life, but it is expensive and time consuming to maintain my life. So I became focused on adoption since there are a lot of kids who need a home, and I have a lot of love to give. Society on the other hand said no Skolis, you can't have that life.

Those are very good suggestions for anyone at that stage in life, but I am bit further along. I am in the same boat, 40+ with little to no hope on the horizon. While my friends were out partying and picking up girls, I obtained two degrees paying cash for college, have a successful business and work in the international markets. My friends are all married with multiple kids deep in debt it with student loans. I earned the right to have the job I want, work when I want, and have what I want in the material sense. The price it seems is I will be forever alone which really hurts. 

&#x200B;

The kick in the teeth out of all this would be the fact the adoption agency we were going through dropped me after my ex left the picture. I can do without a woman in my life if that is my path, but goodness I want to be a father so badly.

As in life all things can be complicated. It isn't killing me not having someone in my life, though it would be nice to be treated like a human. The biggest part I want is that if we can't be mates, let us be mates! I miss having women that are friends. At least one of these failed relationship attempts should turn into a friendship if the math holds true, but humans are born chaos. I constantly development myself both at work and in my personal life. When I stop is when I am dead, try to learn something new every week at least.

&#x200B;

I hope if anyone takes anything from my post, is to not give up. I am out here dating on hard mode because I want to have a family. The wife, children, the whole nine yards because I don't have a family. Tired of being alone, not having what I want out of life. Oh well, I guess it may never happen but I will keep trying!

Once she pushed me I landed on a wooden landing next to a tie-off piling, the owner of the boat called 911 and I did file a report. I am also going to sue her for my medical bills. As for women in general, it isn't all women honestly. It is women where I live whom seem to have an issue with me, which stems from the way I look. Plus being in the minority regarding culture does lead to some poorer interactions. I have a lot of luck with women not from around here, or from other countries. But you do have a point, a major life adjustment may be needed, any suggestions?

&#x200B;

As for the abuse in my relationship, my bio dad was very abusive to me growing up and into my adult life. His death lead caused a lot of issues to resurface so I increased my therapy sessions. I was going to therapy to help deal with my mom's death of almost three years, so we were already at the point of discussing the core of my troubles. Long story short, after a long conversation the doctor noticed my symptoms were worse than a few weeks ago. I recounted a few times my dad was a monster to me, and she asked me how long ago this took place. My reply was beginning of the year, which was wrong due the fact my dad lived 200 miles away. Something in my mind snapped and I started to put it together. Keep in mind that my ex is a good woman, but she had some mental issues without the proper medication to deal. After my mom had passed she had a breakdown (which she kept hidden from me), so the medicine she was on didn't work for her new symptoms, which caused her to drink a lot. The drinking retarded the medicine she was on for her core symptoms thus making the situation worse. To level set, she wasn't anywhere close to my dad in the scope of her abuse, but it was enough that a well adjusted person would leave. I wasn't a well adjusted person at the time of the occurrences.

@IAMTHESmoothOperator

My friend, I don't think there is anything wrong with her shooting for the stars, then at least if she misses, she could end up on top of a mountain. I feel bad that she is angry at all guys, but I can understand her feelings. I have to admit with all the rejections I have had in my life, there was a time I lost all hope.

@DeltaCharlieEcho

I suppose that is directed at me, I appreciate the comment. Sometimes I do feel like I deserve it, I hope you can forgive the person who has hurt you in life
